task: raft-membership
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/raft-membership
worktree: ../okay-wt-mem

why: persist-raft stage 2 lists membership changes and compaction as
  the open halves; the sim harness (raft-sim-fuzz) now makes a
  membership change testable the honest way — a sixth node added and
  one removed under loss and reordering, safety asserted after every
  event — instead of by three hand-written cases.

what: single-server configuration changes (Ongaro's thesis §4.1, the
  variant the paper's authors recommend over joint consensus): a
  config entry in the log, in force from the moment it is appended
  (committed or not), one change at a time (a leader refuses a new
  change while the previous config entry is uncommitted), a removed
  leader steps down once its removal commits. `peers` becomes the
  bootstrap config; majorities, votes and replication run over the
  latest config in the log. Not here: the catch-up (non-voting) phase
  for a joining server, pre-vote against a removed server's
  disruption — both filed if the sim shows them mattering.
